WEBVTT

00:01:27.531 --> 00:01:30.305
But Polly had given me
a very special gift:

00:01:30.305 --> 00:01:32.687
the knowledge that I wasn't alone

00:01:32.687 --> 00:01:36.747
and the realization that abortion
was something that we can talk about.

00:01:37.055 --> 00:01:38.883
Abortion is common.

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:42.678
According to the Guttmacher Institute,
one in three women in America

00:01:42.714 --> 00:01:45.152
will have an abortion in their lifetime.

00:01:48.147 --> 00:01:52.050
But for the last few decades, the dialogue
around abortion in the United States

00:01:52.050 --> 00:01:55.461
has left little room for anything beyond 
pro-life and pro-choice.

00:01:55.944 --> 00:01:58.278
It's political and polarizing.

00:01:58.688 --> 00:02:02.962
But as much as abortion is hotly debated,
it's still rare for us,